  "limitations": [
    "Polar summer only: the sun model keeps the subsolar latitude at -1.54 deg. In polar winter the site gets no sun.",
    "Heater and electronics power have no published source. The shadow heater (50 W) is higher than the whole hibernation draw (43 W), so a survival heater and a working heater are not yet separated.",
    "Hibernation power is calculated from VIPER's 4.2-day darkness survival, so comparing against that figure is not a test. The independent check is the 9.6 h shadow time on 30% of the battery against about 9 h published.",
    "Headlight power has no published source and is swept.",
    "Faults are counted by their average energy cost. A real fault is a whole recovery stop, so worst cases are worse than these numbers. Phase 3 Monte Carlo runs are needed for that.",
    "A return trip uses the sunlight at the moment it starts; the sun moves about 0.5 deg per hour while the rover drives.",
    "Each move uses the conditions of the cell it starts from. A cell counts as sunlit if any part of the sun's disc is visible.",
    "Perception between 105 and 170 deg phase angle is a straight line between the two measured values; Phase 1 has no data there.",
    "One pooled q is used for all terrain. The per-terrain spread is reported as a range on the result, not built into the map.",
    "Slopes from a 5 m DEM are noisy, which makes them read steeper. NASA's slope error map is not used. The rule that a cell is blocked when over half of it is steeper than 25 deg is assumed.",
    "Panel tilt is modelled for the best case only. Battery capacity loss in the cold and the +-3.4% yearly change in sunlight strength are not modelled.",
    "The planner grid is 40 m with 8 neighbours, so routes and reach areas carry grid shape effects.",
    "Rolling resistance and drive efficiency are assumed and swept."
  ],
  "q_provenance": "read from results\\q_model.json"
